id: pm-5gf0xf
title: "Workspace-level point-in-time projection: every read surface answers what the project looked like at time T from history alone"
description: "Promote the single-item pm get --at reconstruction to a workspace-scoped SDK projection primitive consumed by list, search, context, deps, graph, and get --tree, so any past portfolio state is re-derivable from immutable history without hand-replaying streams."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 2
tags[5]: "area:history","area:sdk",context-management,governance,scale
created_at: "2026-07-25T17:47:52.310Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-25T17:59:09.450Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 960
acceptance_criteria: "A public SDK primitive reconstructs the item set, field values, and relationship edges valid at any timestamp or version from history streams plus checkpoint snapshots; --at is accepted on list, search, context, deps, graph, and get --tree with one shared flag contract; the two documented refusals in get.ts (--tree and children projections) are replaced by working support; reads under --at perform zero mutations including usage-ledger writes; a replay gate asserts projected state equals independently recorded state at N past instants including across a history-compact baseline; projection cost is bounded by events-since-checkpoint, not total history; docs cover forensic and audit usage"
