body: "## Rationale\n\n`pm get --at <version|timestamp>` (pm-hib1, shipped PR#549) proves single-item reconstruction works. The workspace-level twin does not exist, and the product says so in its own source:\n\n- `src/cli/commands/get.ts:384` — \"Get --at cannot be combined with --tree because workspace-level historical projections are not yet indexed.\"\n- `src/cli/commands/get.ts:465` — \"Get --at cannot project children because workspace-level historical relationships are not yet indexed.\"\n\nMeasured 2026-07-25: `--at` appears in exactly two flag-contract entries (`flag-contracts.ts:920`, `:1497`); `pm list --at` exits with `Unknown option --at`.\n\nThe immutable history guarantee is only half-delivered while the answer to \"what did this project look like on 2026-03-01\" requires replaying 2,032 streams by hand. Full-proof restoration is an item-scoped promise today and a portfolio-scoped promise in the mandate.\n\n## Scope\n\nOne historical projection primitive in the SDK, consumed by every read surface:\n\n1. `projectWorkspaceAt(ts | version-vector)` — reconstructs the item set, field values, and relationship edges valid at an instant, from history streams plus a bounded cached snapshot ladder.\n2. `--at` accepted uniformly on `list`, `search`, `context`, `deps`, `graph`, and `get --tree` (the two refusals above become real support).\n3. Reads under `--at` stay immutable: no usage-ledger write, no claim side effects, no index mutation beyond the read cache — the `pm get --at` precedent.\n4. Bounded cost: projection uses checkpoint snapshots plus tail replay, so cost scales with events-since-checkpoint, not with total history. Interacts with `pm history-compact` baselines — a compacted stream must still project correctly (its synthetic baseline is a legitimate checkpoint).\n\n## Why this is a platform primitive, not a reporting nicety\n\n- Forensics: \"which items were open when the release cut\" answered from data, not memory.\n- Provable history (pm-w7ccmv): a third party can re-derive any past portfolio state and compare against an attestation bundle (pm-3z0k).\n- Domain platform (pm-t4d7nz): a VCS or digital-twin domain built on pm primitives needs \"state at revision\" as a first-class read, not a per-item loop.\n- Delta reads (pm-tuadp2) are the forward-difference twin: `--since <cursor>` answers \"what changed\", `--at <ts>` answers \"what was true\". Same projection machinery, opposite direction.\n\n## Phasing\n\n1. SDK projection primitive + checkpoint ladder + conformance replay gate.\n2. `list`/`deps`/`get --tree` surfaces (removes the two documented refusals).\n3. `context`/`search`/`graph` under `--at` (relevance scoring against historical candidate sets).\n4. Scale hardening against the pm-801d read index and pm-0qg5 storage fan-out."
